Recommends: 7zip, ghostscript, qpdf, poppler-utils, gir1.2-poppler-0.18, ffmpeg, ffmpegthumbnailer, imagemagick, libheif-plugin-libde265, gnome-sushi,
 ripgrep, zstd, lbzip2, pigz, python3-cairo, python3-gi-cairo, gvfs-backends, xdg-utils
Suggests: brotli, lz4, python3-pypdf, pkexec, gnome-shell-extension-gsconnect
Description: GTK4 file manager in the style of GNOME Files, with built-in tools
 Odysseus looks and behaves like GNOME Files (Nautilus) and follows the
 desktop theme (Adwaita, light/dark, accent colour or installed GTK4 theme).
 It integrates natively the features of the Nautilus extensions by Tof, each
 of which can be switched off without restarting:
  - dual panel, column view, preview panel, tabs;
  - archives (7-Zip engine): browse, extract, compress, split into volumes;
  - PDF tools: compress, merge, watermark, pages;
  - video to audio, image annotation, checksums, content search;
  - "This PC" page, sending files to a phone with GSConnect.
 File operations are designed to never lose data: copies are written under a
 temporary name, originals are removed only once the copy is safely on disk.
